  "worked_solution": "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =-\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(-\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cot}\u2061\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{2}{9}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{9} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot [\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{3})] \\\\ -\\frac{2}{9} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\ -\\frac{2}{9} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
